cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SPACEMAP: a spatial multiplex imaging analysis pipeline"
message: >-
  If you use SPACEMAP in your research, please cite the paper listed under
  preferred-citation.
type: software

# Authors of the SOFTWARE. This is the development credit, and is separate
# from the paper's author list below.
authors:
  - given-names: Bassel
    family-names: Dawod
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Radiation Oncology, University of Texas Southwestern
      Medical Center
    email: basbees@gmail.com
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
  - given-names: Todd
    name-particle: A.
    family-names: Aguilera
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Radiation Oncology, University of Texas Southwestern
      Medical Center
    email: todd.aguilera@utsouthwestern.edu
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"

repository-code: "https://github.com/AguileraLab/SPACEMAP"
url: "https://github.com/AguileraLab/SPACEMAP"
abstract: >-
  SPACEMAP is an end-to-end pipeline for spatial multiplex imaging analysis,
  covering image registration, background subtraction, ROI extraction, tissue
  annotation, cell segmentation, batch correction, immune phenotyping and
  spatial analysis, through a graphical interface and reusable Python modules.
  It includes an optional, local-first AI assistant that is disabled by
  default.
keywords:
  - spatial biology
  - multiplex imaging
  - CODEX
  - cell segmentation
  - phenotyping
  - bioimage analysis
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-09-19"

